ves list, the full 11-card straight **is listed**, meaning it\'s legal and recognized by the system.\n\nBut caution: If I play that massive straight and an opponent bombs even a small part of it (say, a quad 3s or jokers), I lose the lead and may never regain it. Given that each peasant has 17 cards, they likely hold bombs.\n\nMoreover, I hold **♥2 and ♦2**, which are extremely valuable as high singles, and **BlackJoker**, which combines with RedJoker for a rocket — but I don’t have RedJoker, so rocket is impossible. So my jokers are limited.\n\nThus, better to start smaller, test the waters, and preserve key high cards.\n\nAnother idea: **triple_with_single: ♠Q ♣Q ♦Q BlackJoker** uses my strongest single as kicker. But saving BlackJoker for later may be smarter.\n\nBest choice: Start with **triple: ♠4 ♥4 ♣4**. It’s safe, assertive, doesn’t waste high cards, and forces opponents to either spend a rare high triplet (triplet of 2s is highest, then A, K, etc.) or pass. Since triplets above 4 go up to 2, and there are only three 2s total (I have two), it\'s unlikely someone has triplet of 2s (needs three 2s; only one left unknown). So my triple of 4s is likely mid-low, but still, forcing a response now helps reveal information.\n\nAlternatively, **triple_with_pair: ♠4 ♥4 ♣4 ♥2 ♦2** uses both 2s — very powerful, removes six cards, and the pair of 2s is unbeatable (no higher pair than 2s). This is actually a *very* strong play — it’s a "triplet with attached pair", which is a legal combination, and since 2s are the highest pair, no one can beat the pair component unless they bomb.\n\nWait — **this combination cannot be beaten by any other triplet-with-pair**, because the attached pair is 2s, the highest possible. Only a bomb or rocket can beat it.\n\nSo **triple_with_pair: ♠4 ♥4 ♣4 ♥2 ♦2** is a near-optimal opening: it plays five cards (three 4s and two 2s), forms an unmatchable pair attachment, and is highly likely to win the trick outright.\n\nYes — this is stronger than just the triple.\n\nCompare:  \n- Opponent cannot beat it with another triplet+pair unless their attached pair is higher — but nothing beats pair of 2s.  \n- So only way to beat this is with a **bomb** (quad or rocket).  \n- Rocket requires both jokers — I have BlackJoker, so RedJoker alone is useless. No one can have rocket.  \n- So only threat is a **bomb** (four of a kind).\n\nBut bombing this would cost them a valuable bomb early, just to beat a mid-level triplet. Unlikely unless forced.\n\nTherefore, **♠4 ♥4 ♣4 ♥2 ♦2** is a dominant play — it will almost certainly win, clears five cards (including hard-to-dispose 2s), and pressures opponents.\n\nReason: This move uses the highest possible attached pair (2s), making the combination unbeatable except by a bomb. It efficiently disposes of difficult high cards (the 2s are hard to play late) and clears a triplet early. It maximizes pressure on the peasants while minimizing risk.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠4", "♥4", "♣4", "♥2", "♦2"]}'}
